Upstream crosvm files stay under their BSD-3-Clause license (LICENSE).

- DroidVM dvm-crosvm 849e05f (https://github.com/Droid-VM/crosvm, branch droidvm; GPL-2.0-or-later with the permissions
  in ADDITIONAL-PERMISSIONS; GPL text in LICENSE.GPL-2.0): the simple-framebuffer ("--simplefb")
  design -- a framebuffer in host-shared memory just below the static swiotlb, a no-map
  reserved-memory region plus a simple-framebuffer device-tree node, the region shared (not lent)
  on Gunyah, and a host thread that polls it and presents it, with data-cache invalidation before
  each read. Ported in reduced form into aarch64/src/simplefb.rs and
  src/crosvm/sys/linux/simplefb_display.rs, which keep DroidVM's SPDX / copyright header.
  Nothing was taken from the DroidVM app or DroidVM-Daemon repositories.
- DroidVM dvm-crosvm 849e05f, same licence: the VNC display ("--vnc-server", iceland-vms 0.2-7) --
  gpu_display/src/vnc_server_bridge.c, vnc_server_bridge.h and vnc_frame_consumer.h (the LibVNCServer
  bridge: listeners, keysym map, input ring, banded damage tracking, cursor compositing) ported without
  the H.264 path; gpu_display/src/gpu_display_vnc.rs reduced to the CPU transport (no Vulkan blit, no
  H.264 consumer, no dmabuf imports, input through the display's event devices). All keep DroidVM's
  header. Links the system LibVNCServer (GPL-2.0-or-later). The option wiring (src/crosvm/config.rs
  VncConfig, cmdline.rs, sys/linux/gpu.rs, simplefb_display.rs, devices DisplayBackend::Vnc) is our own,
  modelled on DroidVM's.
- DroidVM dvm-crosvm 849e05f, same licence: the pseudo-unprotected memory mode ("--protected-vm-pseudo-unprotected",
